er parts of Anatolia but also from Hurrian Syria and Mesopotamia."  "Hittite religion was an amalgam of elements drawn from various cultural strata: that of the indigenous Hattic people as well as the cultures of the several groups speaking an Anatolian Indo-European language (Hittite, Palaic, or Luwian). To this mix were added influences from Mesopotamia (Babylonia and Assyria) and from the Semitic and Hurrian populations of northern Syria."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 950, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 799})
