l stages of the universe starting with Prajapati-Rudra-Agni and Skanda. His intention must have been to show the local Vedic priests that he knew their world and ambitions.” […] “On the Yodhavade copper series from the region around Kashmir Smats the king can also sit on the elephant. But while he holds a sort of three pronged stick on the gold elephant obverses, he holds up the aspergillum on the Yodhavade coppers. Besides Ardoxsho and Vata this rare copper series shows truly Indian deities – Visakha, Rama, Karttikeya – a late attempt at approaching his Indian subjects? In style and artistic quality these pieces are very different from the older standard coppers of Huviska.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1000, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 887})
