ts made by Mrigesa and other kings show that from the time of this monarch, Jainism became a serious rival of Saiva worship. The flourishing state of Jainism is also indicated by the inscriptions that point to the existence of many communities of Jaina ascetics.”  “This [the Jaina] creed which grew unchecked during the supremacy of the Kadambas, received a fresh stimulus in the time of the Rashtrakutas.”  NB there were also several Jaina ascetics communities during the Kadambas. “The flourishing state of Jainism is also indicated by the inscriptions that point to the existence of many communities of Jaina ascetics, such as the Svetapatas, a sect who were distringuished by their white clothes, the Yāpanias, who weer a sect of religious mendicants, the Kūrchakas, a community of naked religious monks, and the Nirgathas, who wore no clothes at all.”  “The southern ruling powers – Gangas, Kadambas, Chalukyas and Pallavas – also supported Jainism, as various Jaina caves testify.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1060, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 922})
