lim clerics and provided infrastructures for the promotion of Islamic institutions and teachings. The growing business opportunities in the Colony brought many more Muslims from the north, and before long there were small communities of Muslims in and around Freetown, especially in the east end." <br>"While it would be on the margins of the Sierra Leone settlement for the first couple of decades, with the arrival of the Liberated Africans from 1808 onward, Islam moved on to the heart of the Sierra Leone Colony."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 949, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 844})
