hutba, the Friday prayer, and congregational prayer. They observe the precepts of religion, but they have neither madrasa, khanaqah, ribat, nor zawiya.’ The king of Ifat and most of his subjects were shafi’I, the other kingdoms were all Hanafi.” <br>“The most westerly of the Muslim principalities was that of Hadya which covered a very large extent of territory between the rivers of Hawash and Gibe. Its ruling class were Muslim but their subjects who were Sidama and included the semitized Gurage and the Chabo, a fusion of Gurage and Sidama, were pagan.” […] Islam must have declined very rapidly amongst the imperfectly Islamised Sidama for the mass of the people were pagan.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 982, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 852})
