on of the beliefs of the new religion. In the age of Charles Martel most of the peoples among whom the missionaries were active had already been subject to this gradual process for some time, arguably for generations. In areas where they had not, that is, Saxony or in Scandinavia where there was a more resilient, non-Christian culture, the missionaries failed to make much impact and often suffered violent rejection.” .'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 885, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 791})
