olity>'. Was the atlatl, defined as a spear-throwing device used to increase the range and force of a projectile, absent or present as a 'military technology during this time? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: ditch\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of ditch as a military technology used in warfare.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, was the use of ditches as a military technology present or absent in the warfare strategies of '<polity>'? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: chain\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of chainmail as a military technology used in warfare. We’re using a broad definition of chainmail. Habergeon was the word used to describe the Chinese version and that would qualify as chainmail. Armor that is made of small metal rings linked together in a pattern to form a mesh.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, was chainmail, defined as armor made of small metal rings linked together in a pattern to form a mesh, present or absent as a military technology in the warfare practices of '<polity>'? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '"Variable name": Widespread Religion\n"Variable description": “From my sampling of nearly three hundred chronicles, less than a handful of popular revolts appear for the years immediately after the Black Death, and the most prominent of these were initiated by elites rather than artisans or peasants.[...] Despite the rarity of such social revolts, the Black Death nonetheless gave rise to mass movements and violence: flagellant groups and the burning of Jews swept across German-speaking areas, Spain, France and the Low Countries from September 1348 to 1351.” \r\n\r\n"This is probably correct but a very small ‘second most’ and with some caveats worth noting. There are expulsions of the Jews from the French kingdom (ie the part nominally controlled by the king) in 1306 and 1394 etc, although the latter not rigorously enforced. \x0b\x0bProvence has a larger Jewish community, and was not subject to this expulsion order because it was not part of the French kingdom until 1481 - ie after this period. Quite a bit of the scholarly research on Jewish life in late medieval “France” is actually Provence, and French may sometimes be used loosely by scholars.\x0b\x0bIe Pinchas Roth, In this Land: Jewish Life and Legal Culture in Late Medieval Provence (2021)"'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 977, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 844})
