 to temples. The influence of the religion may be seen in the decline of animal sacrifice to heaven, for after the reign of Sheng-tsung, who ruled until 1031, notices of such animal sacrifices practically disappeared. The spirit of compassion was implemented by decrees forbidding the taking of lives on certain fast days, and cremation was now practiced by the Khitans."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 914, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 788})
