l claimed many adherents. Finally, to the south in the Hindukush mountains, in the Kabul valley, Ghazna and in Zamindavar, a resurgence of Hinduism had reasserted Indian influence. Although by the time of Isma\'il b. Ahmad most of Soghdiana was Muslim and Khwarazm much the same, large parts of Bactria, and almost all of the Hindukush and southern Afghanistan regions had not been Islamicized." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 937, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 800})
